# Stakeholder request 1: the learner's landing page is the certification dashboard.
#
# student_dashboard() does
# `if learner_home_mfe_enabled(): return redirect(settings.LEARNER_HOME_MICROFRONTEND_URL)`,
# so pointing that setting at our page and turning the flag on is the whole change.
# The flag is enabled by this plugin's init task. No fork and no core patch.
#
# This lives in the *production* and *development* hooks rather than the common one
# because tutor-mfe sets the same setting from openedx-lms-production-settings,
# which renders after openedx-lms-common-settings and would otherwise overwrite us.
#
# Captured first so the page can link to the real learner dashboard. With tutor-mfe
# enabled this is its MFE URL; without it, None, and the page says so instead of
# linking to /dashboard, which would bounce back here.
NELC_ORIGINAL_LEARNER_HOME_URL = LEARNER_HOME_MICROFRONTEND_URL
LEARNER_HOME_MICROFRONTEND_URL = LMS_ROOT_URL + "/nelc/dashboard/"
